    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 01ea313a195a40bfdc181f74ffa672215266ce12 -->\n**Clean code; conflicts with main (mechanical).**\n\n- **Conflict:** `crates/app/src/commands/operation/gates.rs`, `family_gate`. Main added the #532 wire EDM refusal block where this PR adds the #1291 `mounted`/`clause` lines. Keep both: the wire block first, then `mounted`/`clause`, then the plasma and fallback blocks.\n- **Tests (merged tree):** the quick gate is green (lib 147, plus mcp_order, plasma_profile, refusal_ghost, vertex_pick and wire_contour). `turning` passes 6, `machine_switch` passes 6, and clippy is clean.\n- **Follow-up:** main's new #532 wire refusal still says \"the setup's machine is a mill\" on an unmounted setup, the same flaw this PR fixes. It could use `clause` too. The palette tooltip in `panes.rs` (~L407) is the follow-up already named in the body.\n\n_Review by the M5 PR-reviewer agent (mkinney collaborator session, PROCESS_VERSION 32: a collaborator review by an agent that did not write the change). Trial-merged with upstream main of 2026-11-12 ~21:30Z._\n",
